  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility Study - AIR TRAFFIC CONTROL OFFICER LONG-TERM PLANNING, through Government of India</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USTDA support of $62,160 funds 50 percent of the cost of technical assistance to provide an expert U.S. assessment of the Airport Authority of India&apos;s (AAI) draft Long-Term Manpower Requirements Plan for Air Traffic Control Officers (ATCOs). The hiring and training of new air traffic control officers and the modernization of existing officer capabilities is a critical need for the Grantee, AAI, in maintaining safety standards as it meets its current and anticipated growth and prepares for a major air traffic control modernization program. The project is expected to lead the way to direct procurement of additional U.S. services for manpower assessments, licensing and training programs for the air traffic control sector in India with a special focus on review of manpower requirements for several large, strategic facilities for the aviation sector. This future work would serve as an important first step towards U.S. involvement in the development of these critical facilities with extensive potential for the use of U.S. goods and services.</narrative>
  </description>
